cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  如果您在学术研究、教学或工程中使用了本技能，请引用本仓库。
  If you use this skill in your research, teaching or work, please cite it.
title: monograph-writing
authors:
  - family-names: Chang
    given-names: Sheng
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4935-2766"
    affiliation: Beijing Normal University
    website: "https://github.com/newdeme"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/newdeme/monograph-writing"
abstract: >-
  A batch-writing pipeline for academic monographs, textbooks, technical
  books, and theses, packaged as an Agent Skill for AI writing assistants.
  It turns long-form book writing into small verifiable batches: a
  progress ledger persists all state on disk for seamless continuation
  across sessions and co-authors; an academic red-line system forbids
  fabricated references, classifies contributions (others' published work,
  the author's own published work, unpublished data vs. drafts) with
  dataset freezing and drift tracking; optional thesis-mode tooling covers
  innovation-point registers, blind-review anonymization, and
  plagiarism-check discipline; figures are generated only from the
  author's data files (never invented data points), with Mermaid
  concept-sketch drafts left for the author to redraw; and validation
  scripts check citation numbering, word-count tiers, figure/table
  numbering, and material drift before each batch closes, then generate
  stripped clean copies and a fully-styled merged Word manuscript.
keywords:
  - academic-writing
  - monograph
  - thesis-writing
  - AI-assisted-writing
  - agent-skills
  - writing-pipeline
  - citation-validation
  - research-data-management
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.6.0
date-released: "2026-09-05"
